SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0


WHY CC0

These entries are factual records about published papers. Facts are not
copyrightable; a compilation of them may be. CC0 removes that ambiguity so
anyone can embed, redistribute or build on the registry without asking.

Attribution is requested but NOT required. If you use the registry in published
work, please cite it — see CITATION.cff. Credit here works by scholarly norm
rather than by legal obligation, which is how citation actually functions and
which imposes no barrier on reuse.


WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER

- The software in this repository, which is MIT licensed. See ../LICENSE.
- Quoted data-availability statements, which are short factual quotations from
  the cited papers, used for identification, and remain the property of their
  publishers.
- The underlying papers, corpora and supplementary files referenced by URL.
  Each carries its own license — for example, Genecorpus-30M is Apache-2.0.
  Nothing here relicenses them; the registry records pointers and hashes, not
  redistributed content.
